{
  "version": 3,
  "units": "metres",
  "note": "Positions and sizes are adult dimensions (Guyton & Hall 14e; Standring, Gray's Anatomy 42e), with the origin at roughly the L3 vertebral level, +y towards the head and +z towards the front. THE X AXIS IS THE PATIENT'S: +x is the patient's RIGHT and -x the patient's LEFT, so the liver sits at +x and the stomach, spleen and cardiac apex at -x. A camera in front of the body sees the patient's right on its own left, which is the standard anatomical view; the renderer mirrors x once, at the root of the anatomy (render/scene/Viewer.ts), rather than every file storing screen coordinates. Version 2 of this file was drawn unmirrored and therefore showed a situs inversus - liver on the viewer's right - and three paths in it (the lower oesophagus, the pylorus and the tilt of the heart) had been authored to suit that mirrored picture; they are corrected here. The group offsets are the EXPLODED STACK (spec 6.1): a deliberate design choice, not anatomy, kept in data so it can be animated.",
  "groupLayout": {
    "cranial": {
      "offset": [0, 0.06, 0]
    },
    "thoracic": {
      "offset": [0, 0.0, 0]
    },
    "abdominal": {
      "offset": [0, -0.025, 0]
    },
    "pelvic": {
      "offset": [0, -0.045, 0]
    },
    "axial": {
      "offset": [0, 0, 0]
    }
  },
  "axialWarp": {
    "note": "The exploded stack moves each body region by a rigid offset, which is fine for an organ that lives in one region and wrong for anything that runs through several: the spinal cord, the oesophagus, a ureter, the aorta, the vagus. Those are authored in unexploded body coordinates and bent by this continuous version of the same offsets - zero in the thorax, the cranial offset above the band between `cranial[0]` and `cranial[1]`, the abdominal offset below the diaphragm band, the pelvic offset below the pelvic brim band - so that a vessel still ends at the organ it supplies after that organ has been moved. Organs in the `axial` group carry the warp in their own geometry and take no group offset.",
    "cranial": [0.385, 0.405],
    "abdominal": [0.135, 0.11],
    "pelvic": [-0.135, -0.165]
  },
